{"name":"Ironside","hex":"#7e8082","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ironside","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trooper in the Parliamentarian cavalry formed by English political leader Oliver Cromwell in the 17th century, during the English Civil War."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Old English."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ironside"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ironside (1967 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Ironside is an American television crime drama that aired on NBC over eight seasons from 1967 to 1975. The show starred Raymond Burr as Robert T. Ironside, a consultant to the San Francisco police department, who was paralyzed from the waist down after being shot while on vacation. The character debuted on March 28, 1967, in a TV movie titled Ironside. When the series was broadcast in the United Kingdom, from late 1967 onward, it was broadcast as A Man Called Ironside. The show earned Burr six Emmy and two Golden Globe nominations."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0f/Ironside_Title_Screen.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ironside_(1967_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q892438"},{"title":"Ironside (2013 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Ironside is an American police drama television series created by Collier Young. It aired on NBC from October 2 to October 23, 2013 during the 2013–14 television season. It was a remake of the original television series Ironside, which ran from 1967 to 1975. It starred Blair Underwood as the title character, wheelchair-using cop Robert Ironside, the only character re-created from the original series. The remade Ironside was grittier and considerably more violent than the original, and the setting was changed from San Francisco to New York City."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/60/Ironside_NBC.jpg/330px-Ironside_NBC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ironside_(2013_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q6073242"},{"title":"Ironside (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Ironside is a surname."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ironside_(surname)","wikidata":"Q16871087"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Raymond_burr_ironside.JPG/500px-Raymond_burr_ironside.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Raymond_burr_ironside.JPG/500px-Raymond_burr_ironside.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Raymond Burr as Ironside","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARaymond_burr_ironside.JPG"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey rectangle","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Grey_rectangle.jpg/500px-Grey_rectangle.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_rectangle.jpg","share":0.638125},{"title":"Ironside, OR, abandoned building","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Ironside%2C_OR%2C_abandoned_building.jpg/500px-Ironside%2C_OR%2C_abandoned_building.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ironside,_OR,_abandoned_building.jpg","share":0.33125},{"title":"Grey Bushchat in Sillery Gaon March 2025 by Tisha Mukherjee 01","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg/500px-Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg","ratio":1.3997488488907492,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg","share":0.268125},{"title":"Bernie Hamilton \"Ironside\" (1967 NBC press photo)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Bernie_Hamilton_%22Ironside%2